  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f424be585f9e04c79a96c8292e8b9db1, type: 3}
  m_Name: Conceito_Resiliencia
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Metis.Runtime::KnowledgeEntryData
  _title: "Resili\xEAncia urbana"
  _titleEn: Urban resilience
  _category: 2
  _unlockTrigger: 6
  _summary: "Resili\xEAncia \xE9 a capacidade de uma cidade de aguentar choques,
    como enchentes, apag\xF5es e crises econ\xF4micas, e se recuperar deles. Sobreviver
    aos 20 turnos com eventos imprevis\xEDveis \xE9 um exerc\xEDcio de resili\xEAncia."
  _summaryEn: Resilience is a city's ability to withstand shocks, such as floods,
    blackouts and economic crises, and recover from them. Surviving 20 turns of unpredictable
    events is an exercise in resilience.
  _realWorld: "A rede 100 Resilient Cities, criada pela Funda\xE7\xE3o Rockefeller
    em 2013, ajudou cidades de v\xE1rios continentes a montar planos de resili\xEAncia."
  _realWorldEn: The 100 Resilient Cities network, launched by the Rockefeller Foundation
    in 2013, helped cities on several continents build resilience plans.
  _tradeOffs: "Ter folga e redund\xE2ncia custa dinheiro em tempos normais; o retorno
    s\xF3 aparece na crise."
  _tradeOffsEn: Keeping slack and redundancy costs money in normal times; the payoff
    only shows during a crisis.
  _sources:
  - Label: 100 Resilient Cities (Wikipedia)
    Url: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/100_Resilient_Cities
  - Label: Urban resilience (Wikipedia)
    Url: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Urban_resilience
